   "label": "1667–1669",
   "title": "The Company's ally claims the island",
   "text": "The VOC took Makassar in 1667 with Bugis allies. Bima, until then a tributary of Makassar, became a Company ally under a contract that barred it from trading with other Europeans. Bima's sultans said Sumba had belonged to them since long before any treaty, and Pietrow shows that the VOC repeated this claim in its own letters. Sumba would be reached through Bima, not directly.",
