   "id": "s04",
   "label": "1674–1676",
   "title": "A refused tribute and a fleet turned back",
   "text": "By 1674 part of Sumba refused Bima's tribute. A Bimanese official sold slaves and sappanwood in Batavia for gunpowder, lead and iron, and the VOC promised ships under Adriaan van Dalen. Court quarrels in Bima cut the fleet down. Pietrow reconstructs the result: the joint fleet left Bima on 8 May 1676 and was driven back by a storm on 19 May, while a VOC force coming from Savu turned back with sick crews.",
