   "label": "April–May 1677",
   "title": "Oaths on the kris, and Mamboro waves",
   "text": "The second attempt left Bima on 6 April 1677. The Bimanese landed on 1 May; the VOC ships, ordered to map the island and carrying cloth to trade, arrived on 7 May. Envoys from many villages submitted by drinking water from Bimanese kris. The Dutch left on 17 May, hailed by the people of Mamboro. Hidden rebels then killed two soldiers, panic followed, and the Bimanese fled home by 30 May.",
