   "text": "From Kupang, the VOC post on Timor, the Company tried again on its own account. Hoskins and Soelarto describe an envoy, Van den Burg, agreeing trade terms with eight Sumbanese kings around 1750. Forth records that in 1756 the VOC signed an agreement with the ruler of Mangili, part of the great treaty round that Commissioner Paravicini held in Kupang that year. On paper, Sumba now looked to Kupang.",
