   "text": "Kupang chose a broker rather than an official. Vel describes Sjarif Abdoelrachman, an Arab trader, settling in 1843, taxing horse exports and founding the town that became Waingapu, which Forth also dates to 1843. In 1845 some rajas signed a contract that, in the government's eyes, limited their dealings with outsiders. For three decades the broker, not a Dutchman, stood between Sumba and Kupang.",
