   "text": "In 1901, Forth writes, a Dutch warship anchored off the Rindi estuary during the Lambanapu war, with the Resident of Kupang involved. A campaign of pacification began in 1906; Soelarto describes Lamboya under Umbu Tadu Meli killing Lieutenant de Neeve in 1909. By 1912 Sumba was a colonial afdeeling of the Residency of Timor, divided into sub-departments, each under a noble appointed as zelfbestuurder (raja).",
