   "id": "s20",
   "label": "1978–1990",
   "title": "A crowded field in the west",
   "text": "From the late 1970s West Sumba became one of the most studied places in eastern Indonesia. Kuipers began in the Weyewa highlands in 1978 and Hoskins in Kodi in 1979; Keane worked in Anakalang in the 1980s; Vel lived around Lawonda from 1986 as a development worker; Geirnaert studied the Laboya. Their books shape how Sumba is read today, which is also why this story asks whose voices they carry.",
